table.insert(cors,sandbox(Script399,function()
--[[Airlock v1.0 by WackoMcGoose
To use: Just place it into the Workspace, or as a child of a Model. Put the end
with the warning sign away from whatever kind of space station/ship/whatever
you are making. The end WITHOUT the sign goes inward.

Operation: The green buttons open the door they are next to. If the other door
is open, it closes the other door before opening the first one. The red buttons
close the door they are next to. The airlock does not actually "depressurize".
Instead, walking through one door or the other triggers a certain event. Going
out the outer door gives you low gravity, and will slowly suffocate you if you
are not wearing a space helmet. The inner door will remove the low gravity script
and will let you take off hats as normal.

Hat needed to use: To use the airlock, all you need is a hat named "Space Hat".
Preferrably, you would be wearing the Roblox Astronaut Helmet, but any hat
that is named Space Hat will work. If yu have a custom space helmet in your
place, name it Space Hat for the airlock to work.

Note: If you have NPCs in your place that can walk around (like zombies), the
airlock will also work on them. But since NPCs can't pick up hats (I think...), if
you go through an airlock with zombies chasing you and you're wearing a Space
Hat, the zombie will die. And if you want to change what happens if you go
through without a space helmet, edit the script located at
Airlock.OxygenField.OuterDoor.PutIntoPlayer.SpaceScript
But leave the BrickColorValue "OriginalHeadColor" in the script. It is needed for
the InnerDoor script to work. And if you do edit it, ONLY change the contents of
function NoAir(). LEAVE THE REST OF THE SCRIPT ALONE OR IT WILL LIKELY BREAK.]]
end))
